NativeNovatekTouch (picasso, NT36672C)

NvtTouchCore and NvtProtocol are adapted from ShengNovatekTouch's NT36532E implementation
(https://github.com/UniXNU/NativeNovatekTouch, Apache License 2.0): the core's processing stages, tracking design and
axis-mapping helpers, and the protocol's firmware partition parser, bootloader download flow and 32-byte frame header
integrity checks. This port changes the geometry to 18x36, the register bank to NT36675/NT36672C, and the SPI
addressing to the NT36xxx format. It is distributed under the same license.

GeniSpi.c and GeniSpi.h are vendored from UniXNU/NativeGeniSpi (BSD-2-Clause-Patent); their SPDX headers are unchanged.

The NT36xxx bus facts (page/offset framing, no dummy byte, register bank, chip-info address, trim table and download
sequence) were read from the public sm7150-mainline NT36xxx driver (GPL-2.0-or-later, Novatek/community) and the
sm7250-mainline GCC clock driver proposal. The `hw_crc` firmware-checksum interpretation (golden ILM/DLM values at
0x18/0x1C, `size + 1` partition writes) was confirmed against Google's `kernel/google-modules/touch/novatek_touch`
`nt36xxx_fw_update.c` (GPL-2.0-only). No Linux code is copied.
